※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4588

※ Writing a field writes one place, so what holds the field has to be somewhere.
※ A record the program worked out is a value in registers and has no place for a
※ field to be at; binding it to a name is what gives it one.

type Point = x : u32 ; y : u32

fn made() → Point:
    Point(.x ← 1u32, .y ← 2u32)

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    made().x ← 9u32
    0u6
